course: dictionary
lesson: 9625
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing, and the words around them tell you which meaning to use. Stubbornness is one of these words. It can mean refusing to change your mind, even when there are good reasons. It can also mean determination: not giving up when things are hard.
explain: «The famous stubbornness is really caution: on a rocky desert path, running blindly could mean a fall, so a donkey stops and thinks where a horse would bolt.» The clues are caution and a fall. The donkey's stubbornness keeps it safe, so here it is not a fault.
explain: Stubbornness can also describe things, not just people. The stubbornness of a stain means it is hard to remove. Ask yourself: is this a person, a thing, or a sensible pause? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Stubbornness is a noun: it names a quality that a person or thing can have.
fact: Stubbornness means refusing to change your mind or do what others want, even when there are good reasons.
fact: Stubbornness can also mean determination: not giving up when things are hard.
fact: «The famous stubbornness is really caution» shows that something that looks like stubbornness can be a sensible pause.
fact: People say "out of stubbornness", "sheer stubbornness" and "stubbornness of a mule", because mules are thought of as stubborn.
exercise: «The famous stubbornness is really caution: on a rocky desert path, running blindly could mean a fall.» What does the donkey's stubbornness show here? | *Caution, a sensible pause before danger | A wish to run as fast as it can | Laziness, because it does not want to walk | Illness, because it cannot see well
exercise: Mia kept practising her times tables every day, even when they were hard. What does her stubbornness mean here? | Being unkind to her teacher | Being very quiet in class | Refusing to ever try again | *Determination: not giving up when things are hard
exercise: «The stubbornness of the stain stayed even after washing.» What does the stubbornness of the stain mean? | It was wet and cold | It smelled of flowers | It was very bright and colourful | *It was hard to remove
exercise: Ben would not wear his coat, even when the rain came. What does «out of stubbornness» suggest? | He was cold and needed help | It was his birthday | His coat was lost | *He refused to change his mind
exercise: Which phrase compares stubbornness to an animal? | Out of joy | *Stubbornness of a mule | Bright as a star | Sheer kindness
test: Dad would not change his mind, even after Sam showed him good reasons. Which meaning of stubbornness fits? | Not giving up when things are hard | *Refusing to change your mind, even with good reasons | Being very tired after a long walk | Shining brightly in the dark
test: Why might the word stubbornness be a good thing in a story? | *Because it can mean determination, not giving up when things are hard | Because it means you never need to think | Because it is the same as being lost | Because it always means kindness and love
exam: «She showed great stubbornness in finishing the race, even when her legs ached.» Which meaning fits best? | Being unkind to the other runners | Refusing ever to run again | A stain that is hard to wash out | *Determination: not giving up when things are hard
